  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive sample <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> having the activity <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has twice the number of nuclei as another sample <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> of activity<math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>. If <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> then the ratio of half-life of <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to the half-life of <math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is",
